# Spec for tools/riscpkg.py: the WebP plug-in for Lumen.
Package: LumenWebP
Section: Graphics
Priority: Optional
Licence: Free
Maintainer: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Standards-Version: 0.4.0
Environment: arm32, vfpv3
Depends: Lumen (>= 0.0.37)
Homepage: https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-lumen
Description: WebP pictures in Lumen
 The LumenWebP plug-in lets Lumen open WebP pictures (.webp), lossy and
 lossless, with or without transparency (laid on white); for an
 animated WebP, the first frame. Built from libwebp 1.6.0, using NEON
 where the processor has it. It goes into Lumen's Plugins directory,
 with its own guide.
Build-Map: !Lumen/Plugins/WebP -> Apps/Graphics/!Lumen/Plugins/WebP
Build-Notice: LumenWebP, packaged for PackMan from the release zip on
 https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-lumen/releases
 .
 LumenWebP's own code is under the MIT licence. libwebp 1.6.0 (BSD
 3-clause, Copyright (c) 2010 Google Inc., with Google's patent grant)
 is built into it. The notices follow.
Build-Copyright: !Lumen/Plugins/WebP/Licence
